The legal texts are laws of Turkmenistan, as published by the Mejlis of Turkmenistan (Türkmenistanyň Mejlisi)
at https://mejlis.gov.tm, retrieved 28 October 2026.

The Mejlis site carries the line "Ähli hukuklar goralan" (all rights reserved) for the site as a whole.
The laws themselves are not protected by copyright in Turkmenistan: Article 7 of the Law of Turkmenistan
"On Copyright and Related Rights" (Zakon "Ob avtorskom prave i smezhnykh pravakh", No. 257-IV of 10 January 2012,
as amended) lists among the works that are not objects of copyright "официальные документы (законы, судебные
решения, иные тексты законодательного, административного ..." (the quotation is cut there), and their official translations
(official documents: laws, court decisions and other texts of a legislative, administrative and judicial nature).
Source of the clause: WIPO Lex, Russian text of the law.

Changes made by Lexifina: each text was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per line;
spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised; superscript article numbers were written as hyphenated numbers; and
the versions were arranged as git commits credited to the laws that made them. The wording of the law was not
changed. The Mejlis does not endorse this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the
tools) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
